6. Opening-Balance Migration and Revision Strategy (Issue 2.C)
Strict Plausible Opening-Candidate Rule (No Manual-Adjustment False Positives):
An entry e is a plausible opening-balance candidate for account acc iff:
e.entryType == 'adjustment' AND (e.id.startsWith('entry-open-') || e.description.startsWith('Opening Balance') || e.legacySourceTxId == 'open:${acc.id}' || e.legacySourceTxId?.startsWith('open:${acc.id}:rev:') == true) AND (e touches acc.id OR legacySourceTxId names acc.id).
Ordinary manual adjustments (e.g., 'Cash Count Adjustment') are strictly excluded so they never block migration or get flagged.
Exact 7 Verification Criteria + 5-Case Migration Outcomes (V7LedgerHardener):
Criteria: (1) exact acc.id signed balance == acc.openingBalanceCents, (2) correct Dr/Cr direction, (3) exact abs amount with clean equity offset, (4) >= 2 postings & Dr == Cr, (5) isVoided == false, (6) valid opening type/marker, (7) legacySourceTxId == null or matches 'open:${acc.id}'/:rev:n.
Case 1 (Conflicting non-opening legacySourceTxId) -> Preserve untouched & flag OPENING_CONFLICTING_LEGACY_LINK.
Case 2 (0 plausible active candidates & openingBalanceCents != 0 & no broken candidate) -> Synthesize single opening entry ('open:${acc.id}')—never duplicating when a valid entry exists!
Case 3 (Exactly 1 valid candidate passing 1–7) -> Match idempotently (matchedOpeningBalances).
Case 4 (>= 2 valid candidates passing 1–7) -> Preserve all untouched & flag OPENING_MULTIPLE_CANDIDATES (zero silent deletions/merges).
Case 5 (>= 1 non-superseded plausible candidate failing 1–7) -> Preserve untouched & flag OPENING_INCONSISTENT_CANDIDATE with exact failing criterion codes (never auto-create a duplicate entry). Superseded voided :rev:n entries chained via correctedFromEntryId to a valid active opening entry are recognized as valid edit history, not errors.
Immutable :rev:{n} Provenance on User Edits (DriftFinanceRepository):
First opening entry uses legacySourceTxId = 'open:${account.id}'.
Every subsequent edit computes n = maxExistingRevision + 1, marks prior active opening entry isVoided = true, voidReason = 'Updated opening balance' without clearing legacySourceTxId, postings, amount, or date, and (when new balance != 0) inserts 'open:${account.id}:rev:$n' referencing correctedFromEntryId = previousEntry.id.
Editing opening balance to 0 voids the active opening entry; restoring non-zero later creates 'open:${account.id}:rev:${n+1}' chaining from the latest voided revision, guaranteeing exact 1x balance counting and unbroken provenance.
