8. Foreign-Key and SQLite TableMigration Rebuild Procedure (Issue 2.B)
8.1 Universal SQLite ON DELETE RESTRICT + App Lifecycle Policy
Every finance FK uses ON DELETE RESTRICT in SQLite (PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON enabled in beforeOpen), preventing silent CASCADE deletions or SET NULL side effects, while application services enforce relationship-specific behavior:
Never hard-deleted: JournalEntriesTable, PostingsTable, DebtsTable, SettlementAllocationsTable, CommitmentSettlementsTable (after creation), FinancialTransactions (use voiding / immutable records).
Archive instead of delete once referenced: AccountsTable, FinancialCategories, PartiesTable, RecurringRulesTable (once rules have generated commitments/rec:* entries, pause via isActive = false; unused rules delete freely).
Explicit App Unlink Permitted (UPDATE ... SET col = NULL, never DELETE side effect): FinancialCommitments.linkedAccountId, FinancialCommitments.categoryId, FinancialCommitments.linkedDebtId (unpaid draft only), RecurringRulesTable.{accountId, destinationAccountId, categoryId, linkedDebtId} (Edit Rule), FinancialCategories.parentId (promote subcategory to top-level), and SavingsGoals.linkedAccountId (explicitly gated on 0 balance/allocation).
Unused Draft Delete Permitted: Unpaid commitments (0 settlements & !legacyPaidUnverified), individual BudgetsTable rows, unreferenced accounts/categories/parties/rules, and virtual SavingsGoals (currentAllocatedCents == 0).
8.2 Valid SQLite & Drift Transaction Table-Rebuild Procedure
[Proposed engineering decision] Because SQLite ignores PRAGMA foreign_keys toggles inside an active transaction:
Transaction Boundary Invariant: Never enable PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON in any NativeDatabase(..., setup: ...) hook before beforeOpen; confirm via SELECT foreign_keys at entry of from < 7 that foreign_keys == 0 while onUpgrade runs inside Drift's upgrade transaction (throw LedgerMigrationException immediately before DDL if a misconfigured test harness pre-enabled it!).
Pre-Rebuild Orphan Hygiene (For Un-FK'd v6 Columns): Before adding ON DELETE RESTRICT constraints via rebuilds, clean pre-v7 dangling FinancialCommitments.recurring_rule_id (SET NULL + log ORPHANED_RECURRING_RULE_LINK_CLEARED) and dangling FinancialCategories.parent_id (SET NULL + log ORPHANED_CATEGORY_PARENT_CLEARED) so existing v6 data passes PRAGMA foreign_key_check.
Strict Topological Rebuild Order (Parents Before Children — Level 0 -> Level 3):
(Prevents SQLite 12-step ALTER TABLE parent RENAME from leaving child tables referencing temp names!)
Level 0: financial_categories, accounts_table, parties_table, journal_entries_table.
Level 1: postings_table, debts_table (adds write_off_entry_id, normalizes writtenOff/voided), savings_goals (adds status), budgets_table, financial_transactions.
Level 2: settlement_allocations_table, recurring_rules_table, financial_commitments (adds direction, legacy_paid_unverified; rebuilt after recurring_rules_table, debts_table, accounts_table, financial_categories, journal_entries_table).
Level 3: commitment_settlements_table (created cleanly referencing final v7 financial_commitments and journal_entries_table).
Re-Create All Performance Indices: Immediately after TableMigration rebuilds, re-create every CREATE [UNIQUE] INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ... (which TableMigration drops on rebuilt tables!).
Audit & Commit Check: Run V7LedgerHardener.hardenAndAuditInTransaction(this) -> verify PRAGMA foreign_key_check returns zero rows inside onUpgrade (throw LedgerMigrationException to roll back on any failure). After onUpgrade commits, beforeOpen activates PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON cleanly.
9. Safe Raw Database Recovery Sequence (Issue 2.D)
Detect & Classify Failure (AppStateManager._runInitialize()): Distinguish LedgerMigrationException (logical migration/invariant rollback), DatabaseCorruptionException (SQLITE_CORRUPT/SQLITE_NOTADB or PRAGMA quick_check(1) fail), and File-System I/O (FileSystemException/disk full/lock).
Block App Initialization: Keep isInitialized = false; never load repositories, controllers, or recurring jobs.
Dispose Failed Connection First: Always await _db.close() (guarded by try/catch + bounded timeout) before inspecting or touching .sqlite files on disk so background isolate handles release cleanly.
Inspect WAL & SHM Sidecars Cold: While closed, inspect personal_management.sqlite, personal_management.sqlite-wal, and personal_management.sqlite-shm. Never open a failed/corrupt DB to checkpoint WAL or run VACUUM INTO, and never copy .sqlite without its -wal/-shm sidecars!
Persist External Diagnostic Atomic Fallback: Write sanitized failure JSON via .tmp -> rename to migration_last_failure.json alongside app support dir; if disk-full/permission error prevents writing the file, retain full JSON in AppStateManager.initializationFailure memory so UI diagnostics remain intact.
Cold Raw Copy & Verification (RawDatabaseRecoveryExporter, Zero Drift): Using pure dart:io while DB is closed, stage .sqlite + existing -wal/-shm + migration_last_failure.json + a manifest.json (recording exact filenames, byte sizes, and SHA-256 checksums computed before export) into a .zip/folder at the user's chosen destination, verify written bundle files exist with matching byte sizes/SHA-256, and show explicit confirmation; if export fails, preserve original failure state & live files untouched.
Recovery Actions on DaywellShellStatusView (Zero DB Queries):
Invariant / Transient I/O Failure: Prompt Export Raw DB Backup (strongly recommended after attemptCount >= 2) and allow Retry Upgrade.
Corrupt SQLite File: Suppress blind retry; offer Export Raw DB Backup + Restore Encrypted .daywell Backup (double confirmation).
Quarantine & Verified Restoration Sequence: Move damaged .sqlite, -wal, and -shm atomically into recovery_quarantine/<timestamp>/; instantiate fresh AppDatabase; execute importSnapshot in 1 transaction + PRAGMA foreign_key_check; delete quarantine only after verified v7 commit (restoring quarantine automatically if import aborts).
Controlled Reopen: Delete migration_last_failure.json only after ensureInitialized() succeeds cleanly at user_version = 7, then hydrate controllers into DaywellAppShell.
